IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 29/6/2026 to 20/10/2026" (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (2) -- s 242: stop order for a prospectus and profile statement. LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- Reading a result (the rule of 2026-10-29): JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is "the TEXT says no in its own words"; NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Every "no" branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`, every "not covered" branch `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
-- The Authority's opinions (s 242(1)(a), (c), (d) and (2)(a), (c), (d)) are INPUTS: a fact the person states about what the Authority has said.
-- Deadlines: "within 14 days from the date of the stop order" is a deadline, so an act on the day of the stop order is in time (fork F9).
-- A duty is answered as "has the person done what the text requires" (fork F18); a "where" paragraph first as "is the person bound by it" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)).

-- inert (reason 1), lines 39581-39581: s 242 marginal heading: not operative.

§ `s 242(1) and (2): the stop order`

DECLARE `s 242 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 242(11) allot, issue or sell securities or securities-based derivatives contracts contrary to the order`

-- s 242(1): the Authority may serve a stop order for a registered prospectus. A power whose "If" gate may fail: NOTHING (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit (1); fork F22).
-- src:39583 | 242.—(1) If a prospectus has been registered and —
-- src:39585 | (a) the Authority is of the opinion that the prospectus contains
-- src:39586 | a false or misleading statement;
-- src:39588 | (b) there is an omission from the prospectus of any
-- src:39589 | information that is required to be included in it under
-- src:39590 | section 243;
-- src:39592 | (c) the Authority is of the opinion that the prospectus does not
-- src:39593 | comply with the requirements of this Act; or
-- src:39595 | (d) the Authority is of the opinion that it is in the public
-- src:39596 | interest to do so,
-- src:39598 | the Authority may by a written order (called in this section a stop
-- src:39599 | order) served on the person making the offer of securities or
-- src:39600 | securities‑based derivatives contracts to which the prospectus relates
-- src:39605 | direct that no or no further securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:39606 | contracts be allotted, issued or sold.
@ref s 242(1) (src:39583-39606)
GIVEN
    `the prospectus has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prospectus been registered?
    `the Authority is of the opinion that the prospectus contains a false or misleading statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that the prospectus contains a false or misleading statement?
    `there is an omission from the prospectus of any information that is required to be included in it under section 243` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an omission from the prospectus of any information that is required to be included in it under section 243?
    `the Authority is of the opinion that the prospectus does not comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that the prospectus does not comply with the requirements of the Securities and Futures Act?
    `the Authority is of the opinion that it is in the public interest to serve a stop order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that it is in the public interest to serve a stop order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F22 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 242(1) the Authority may serve a stop order on the person making the offer for the prospectus` MEANS
    IF `the prospectus has been registered` AND (`the Authority is of the opinion that the prospectus contains a false or misleading statement` OR `there is an omission from the prospectus of any information that is required to be included in it under section 243` OR `the Authority is of the opinion that the prospectus does not comply with the requirements of this Act` OR `the Authority is of the opinion that it is in the public interest to serve a stop order`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a prospectus has been registered and (a) the Authority is of the opinion that the prospectus contains a false or misleading statement; ... the Authority may by a written order (called in this section a stop order) served on the person making the offer"  -- GRANT-RULING (1): an "if" gate failed on a function named for a power; the other reading is JUST FALSE

-- s 242(2): the same for a registered profile statement.
-- src:39610 | (2) If a profile statement has been registered and —
-- src:39612 | (a) the Authority is of the opinion that the profile statement
-- src:39613 | contains a false or misleading statement;
-- src:39615 | (b) there is an omission from the profile statement of any
-- src:39616 | information that is required to be included in it under
-- src:39617 | section 246;
-- src:39619 | (c) the Authority is of the opinion that the profile statement
-- src:39620 | does not comply with the requirements of this Act; or
-- src:39622 | (d) the Authority is of the opinion that it is in the public
-- src:39623 | interest to do so,
-- src:39625 | the Authority may by a written order (called in this section a stop
-- src:39626 | order) served on the person making the offer of securities or
-- src:39627 | securities‑based derivatives contracts to which the profile statement
-- src:39628 | relates direct that no or no further securities or securities‑based
-- src:39629 | derivatives contracts be allotted, issued or sold.
@ref s 242(2) (src:39610-39629)
GIVEN
    `the profile statement has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the profile statement been registered?
    `the Authority is of the opinion that the profile statement contains a false or misleading statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that the profile statement contains a false or misleading statement?
    `there is an omission from the profile statement of any information that is required to be included in it under section 246` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an omission from the profile statement of any information that is required to be included in it under section 246?
    `the Authority is of the opinion that the profile statement does not comply with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that the profile statement does not comply with the requirements of the Securities and Futures Act?
    `the Authority is of the opinion that it is in the public interest to serve a stop order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that it is in the public interest to serve a stop order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F22 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 242(2) the Authority may serve a stop order on the person making the offer for the profile statement` MEANS
    IF `the profile statement has been registered` AND (`the Authority is of the opinion that the profile statement contains a false or misleading statement` OR `there is an omission from the profile statement of any information that is required to be included in it under section 246` OR `the Authority is of the opinion that the profile statement does not comply with the requirements of this Act` OR `the Authority is of the opinion that it is in the public interest to serve a stop order`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a profile statement has been registered and (a) the Authority is of the opinion that the profile statement contains a false or misleading statement; ... the Authority may by a written order (called in this section a stop order) served on the person making the offer"  -- GRANT-RULING (1): an "if" gate failed on a function named for a power; the other reading is JUST FALSE

-- s 242(3): the Authority must not serve a stop order once the securities are listed and trading has begun. "if" is the bar's own condition: a failed "if" is the text's no (reading (a)), and the bar is limited by its own wording (SPLIT-SITE (i)).
-- src:39633 | (3) Despite subsections (1) and (2), the Authority must not serve a
-- src:39634 | stop order if any of the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:39635 | contracts to which the prospectus or profile statement relates has been
-- src:39636 | issued or sold, and listed for quotation on an approved exchange and
-- src:39637 | trading in them has commenced.
@ref s 242(3) (src:39633-39637)
GIVEN
    `any of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts has been issued or sold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to which the prospectus or profile statement relates been issued or sold?
    `any of them has been listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any of them been listed for quotation on an approved exchange?
    `trading in them has commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has trading in them commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F23 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 242(3) the Authority must not serve a stop order` MEANS
    IF `any of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts has been issued or sold` AND `any of them has been listed for quotation on an approved exchange` AND `trading in them has commenced`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Authority must not serve a stop order if any of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to which the prospectus or profile statement relates has been issued or sold, and listed for quotation on an approved exchange and trading in them has commenced"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- s 242(4): the Authority must give the person making the offer an opportunity to be heard, except on the public-interest grounds listed.
-- src:39641 | (4) The Authority must not serve a stop order under subsection (1)
-- src:39642 | or (2) without giving the person making the offer an opportunity to be
-- src:39643 | heard, except that an opportunity to be heard need not be given if the
-- src:39644 | stop order is served on the ground that it is in the public interest to do
-- src:39645 | so on the basis of any of the following circumstances:
-- src:39647 | (a) the person making the offer (being an entity), the issuer or
-- src:39648 | the trustee‑manager of the business trust or, where
-- src:39649 | applicable, the underlying entity or the business trust is
-- src:39650 | in the course of being wound up or otherwise dissolved,
-- src:39651 | whether in Singapore or elsewhere;
-- src:39656 | (aa) the person making the offer (being an individual) is an
-- src:39657 | undischarged bankrupt, whether in Singapore or
-- src:39658 | elsewhere;
-- src:39660 | (b) a receiver, a receiver and manager or an equivalent person
-- src:39661 | has been appointed, whether in Singapore or elsewhere, in
-- src:39662 | relation to or in respect of —
-- src:39664 | (i) any property of the person making the offer (being an
-- src:39665 | entity), the issuer or, where applicable, the
-- src:39666 | underlying entity;
-- src:39668 | (ii) any property of the trustee‑manager of the business
-- src:39669 | trust; or
-- src:39671 | (iii) the trust property of the business trust.
@ref s 242(4) (src:39641-39671)
GIVEN
    `a stop order is to be served under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a stop order to be served on you under section 242(1) or (2)?
    `the stop order is served on the ground that it is in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the stop order served on the ground that it is in the public interest to do so?
    `the person making the offer (being an entity), the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust or, where applicable, the underlying entity or the business trust is in the course of being wound up or otherwise dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person making the offer (being an entity), the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust or, where applicable, the underlying entity or the business trust in the course of being wound up or otherwise dissolved, whether in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the person making the offer (being an individual) is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person making the offer (being an individual) an undischarged bankrupt, whether in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `a receiver, a receiver and manager or an equivalent person has been appointed in relation to property of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity, the trustee-manager or the trust property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a receiver, a receiver and manager or an equivalent person been appointed, whether in Singapore or elsewhere, in relation to any property of the person making the offer (being an entity), the issuer or, where applicable, the underlying entity, any property of the trustee-manager of the business trust, or the trust property of the business trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(4) the Authority must give the person making the offer an opportunity to be heard` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a stop order is to be served under subsection (1) or (2)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Authority must not serve a stop order under subsection (1) or (2) without giving the person making the offer an opportunity to be heard"
        IF `the stop order is served on the ground that it is in the public interest` AND (`the person making the offer (being an entity), the issuer, the trustee-manager of the business trust or, where applicable, the underlying entity or the business trust is in the course of being wound up or otherwise dissolved` OR `the person making the offer (being an individual) is an undischarged bankrupt` OR `a receiver, a receiver and manager or an equivalent person has been appointed in relation to property of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity, the trustee-manager or the trust property`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that an opportunity to be heard need not be given if the stop order is served on the ground that it is in the public interest to do so on the basis of any of the following circumstances"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `s 242(5) and (6): applicants to subscribe, when a stop order is served`

-- s 242(5)(a): the "where" gate (applications to subscribe made before the stop order; the securities not issued): JUST FALSE when it fails (periods ruling, rule (b)).
-- src:39675 | (5) Where applications to subscribe for securities or
-- src:39676 | securities‑based derivatives contracts to which the prospectus or
-- src:39677 | profile statement relates have been made prior to the stop order,
-- src:39678 | then —
-- src:39680 | (a) where the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:39681 | contracts have not been issued to the applicants —
@ref s 242(5)(a) (the gate) (src:39675-39681)
GIVEN
    `applications to subscribe for the securities or contracts have been made prior to the stop order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were applications to subscribe for securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to which the prospectus or profile statement relates made before the stop order?
    `the securities or contracts have not been issued to the applicants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts not yet been issued to the applicants?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(5)(a) the person making the offer is bound by paragraph (a)` MEANS
    IF `applications to subscribe for the securities or contracts have been made prior to the stop order` AND `the securities or contracts have not been issued to the applicants`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where applications to subscribe for securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to which the prospectus or profile statement relates have been made prior to the stop order, then (a) where the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts have not been issued to the applicants"

-- src:39683 | (i) the applications are deemed to have been withdrawn
-- src:39684 | and cancelled; and
@ref s 242(5)(a)(i) (src:39683-39684)
GIVEN
    `applications to subscribe for the securities or contracts have been made prior to the stop order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were applications to subscribe for securities or securities-based derivatives contracts made before the stop order?
    `the securities or contracts have not been issued to the applicants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts not yet been issued to the applicants?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(5)(a)(i) the applications are deemed to have been withdrawn and cancelled` MEANS
    IF `applications to subscribe for the securities or contracts have been made prior to the stop order` AND `the securities or contracts have not been issued to the applicants`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where applications to subscribe for securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to which the prospectus or profile statement relates have been made prior to the stop order ... where the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts have not been issued to the applicants (i) the applications are deemed to have been withdrawn and cancelled"

-- src:39686 | (ii) the person making the offer must, within 14 days
-- src:39687 | from the date of the stop order, pay to the applicants
-- src:39688 | all moneys the applicants have paid on account of
-- src:39689 | their applications for the securities or
-- src:39690 | securities‑based derivatives contracts; or
@ref s 242(5)(a)(ii) (src:39686-39690)
GIVEN
    `the date of the stop order` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the stop order served?
    `the person making the offer paid the applicants all moneys they paid on account of their applications` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay the applicants all the moneys they paid on account of their applications for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the date the moneys were paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you pay the applicants?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(5)(a)(ii) the person making the offer has paid the applicants within 14 days from the date of the stop order` MEANS
    IF `the person making the offer paid the applicants all moneys they paid on account of their applications` AND (`the date the moneys were paid` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the stop order` 14 Days))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the person making the offer must, within 14 days from the date of the stop order, pay to the applicants all moneys the applicants have paid on account of their applications for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts"

-- s 242(5)(b): securities issued to the applicants.
-- src:39692 | (b) where the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:39693 | contracts have been issued to the applicants —
-- src:39695 | (i) the issue of the securities or securities‑based
-- src:39696 | derivatives contracts is deemed to be void; and
@ref s 242(5)(b) (the gate) (src:39692-39696)
GIVEN
    `applications to subscribe for the securities or contracts have been made prior to the stop order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were applications to subscribe for securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to which the prospectus or profile statement relates made before the stop order?
    `the securities or contracts have been issued to the applicants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts been issued to the applicants?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(5)(b) the person making the offer is bound by paragraph (b)` MEANS
    IF `applications to subscribe for the securities or contracts have been made prior to the stop order` AND `the securities or contracts have been issued to the applicants`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where applications to subscribe for securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to which the prospectus or profile statement relates have been made prior to the stop order, then ... (b) where the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts have been issued to the applicants"

@ref s 242(5)(b)(i) (src:39695-39696)
GIVEN
    `applications to subscribe for the securities or contracts have been made prior to the stop order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were applications to subscribe for securities or securities-based derivatives contracts made before the stop order?
    `the securities or contracts have been issued to the applicants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts been issued to the applicants?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(5)(b)(i) the issue of the securities or contracts is deemed to be void` MEANS
    IF `applications to subscribe for the securities or contracts have been made prior to the stop order` AND `the securities or contracts have been issued to the applicants`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts have been issued to the applicants (i) the issue of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts is deemed to be void"

-- src:39698 | (ii) the person making the offer must, within 14 days
-- src:39699 | from the date of the stop order, pay to the applicants
-- src:39704 | all moneys paid by them for the securities or
-- src:39705 | securities‑based derivatives contracts.
@ref s 242(5)(b)(ii) (src:39698-39705)
GIVEN
    `the date of the stop order` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the stop order served?
    `the person making the offer paid the applicants all moneys they paid for the securities or contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay the applicants all the moneys they paid for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the date the moneys were paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you pay the applicants?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(5)(b)(ii) the person making the offer has paid the applicants within 14 days from the date of the stop order` MEANS
    IF `the person making the offer paid the applicants all moneys they paid for the securities or contracts` AND (`the date the moneys were paid` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the stop order` 14 Days))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the person making the offer must, within 14 days from the date of the stop order, pay to the applicants all moneys paid by them for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts"

-- s 242(6): subsection (5)(b) has effect despite the Companies Act 1967.
