-- src:39746 | securities‑based derivatives contracts; or
@ref s 242(7)(b)(i) (src:39733-39746)
GIVEN
    `documents purporting to evidence title to the securities or contracts have been issued to the applicants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have documents purporting to evidence title to the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts been issued to the applicants?
    `the date of the stop order` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the stop order served?
    `the person informed the applicants to return the documents within 14 days from the date of the stop order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you inform the applicants to return the documents to you within 14 days from the date of the stop order?
    `the date the applicants were informed` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you inform the applicants?
    `the date the documents were received` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive the documents (any date if none was received)?
    `the person making the offer paid the applicants all moneys they paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay the applicants all the moneys they paid for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the date the moneys were paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you pay the applicants?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(7)(b)(i) the person making the offer has informed the applicants and paid them, where title documents were issued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `documents purporting to evidence title to the securities or contracts have been issued to the applicants`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(i) if documents purporting to evidence title to the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts have been issued to the applicants"
        IF `the person informed the applicants to return the documents within 14 days from the date of the stop order` AND (`the date the applicants were informed` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the stop order` 7 Days)) AND `the person making the offer paid the applicants all moneys they paid` AND (`the date the moneys were paid` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` (IF `the date the documents were received` AT LEAST `the date of the stop order` THEN `the date the documents were received` ELSE `the date of the stop order`) 7 Days))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(A) within 7 days from the date of the stop order, inform the applicants to return such documents to the person making the offer within 14 days from that date; and (B) within 7 days from the date of the receipt of those documents or the date of the stop order, whichever is the later, pay to the applicants all moneys paid by them for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts"

-- src:39751 | (ii) if no such documents have been issued to the
-- src:39752 | applicants, within 7 days from the date of the stop
-- src:39753 | order, pay to the applicants all moneys paid by them
-- src:39754 | for the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:39755 | contracts.
@ref s 242(7)(b)(ii) (src:39751-39755)
GIVEN
    `documents purporting to evidence title to the securities or contracts have been issued to the applicants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have documents purporting to evidence title to the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts been issued to the applicants?
    `the date of the stop order` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the stop order served?
    `the person making the offer paid the applicants all moneys they paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay the applicants all the moneys they paid for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the date the moneys were paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you pay the applicants?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(7)(b)(ii) the person making the offer has paid the applicants within 7 days, where no title documents were issued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `documents purporting to evidence title to the securities or contracts have been issued to the applicants`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(ii) if no such documents have been issued to the applicants"
        IF `the person making the offer paid the applicants all moneys they paid` AND (`the date the moneys were paid` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the stop order` 7 Days))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) if no such documents have been issued to the applicants, within 7 days from the date of the stop order, pay to the applicants all moneys paid by them for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts"

§ `s 242(8) to (10): the interim stop order`

-- s 242(8): the Authority may serve an interim stop order without a hearing. A power with an "If" gate: NOTHING when it fails (grant ruling, fork F22).
-- src:39759 | (8) If the Authority is of the opinion that any delay in serving a stop
-- src:39760 | order pending the holding of a hearing required under subsection (4)
-- src:39761 | is not in the interests of the public, the Authority may, without giving
-- src:39762 | an opportunity to be heard, serve an interim stop order on the person
-- src:39763 | making the offer directing that no or no further securities or
-- src:39764 | securities‑based derivatives contracts to which the prospectus or
-- src:39765 | profile statement relates be allotted, issued or sold.
@ref s 242(8) (src:39759-39765)
GIVEN
    `the Authority is of the opinion that any delay in serving a stop order pending the holding of a hearing required under subsection (4) is not in the interests of the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that any delay in serving a stop order, pending the holding of a hearing required under section 242(4), is not in the interests of the public?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F22 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 242(8) the Authority may serve an interim stop order without giving an opportunity to be heard` MEANS
    IF `the Authority is of the opinion that any delay in serving a stop order pending the holding of a hearing required under subsection (4) is not in the interests of the public`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Authority is of the opinion that any delay in serving a stop order pending the holding of a hearing required under subsection (4) is not in the interests of the public, the Authority may, without giving an opportunity to be heard, serve an interim stop order"  -- GRANT-RULING (1): an "if" gate failed on a function named for a power; the other reading is JUST FALSE

-- s 242(9): how long an interim stop order is in force. "unless revoked" is a closed gate; "until" ends it when the Authority makes an order; in any other case 14 days beginning with the day it is served (the keel's P10; fork F24).
-- src:39769 | (9) An interim stop order, unless revoked by the Authority, is in
-- src:39770 | force —
-- src:39772 | (a) in a case where —
-- src:39774 | (i) it is served during a hearing under subsection (4); or
-- src:39776 | (ii) a hearing under subsection (4) is commenced while it
-- src:39777 | is in force,
-- src:39779 | (a) until the Authority makes an order under subsection (1) or
-- src:39780 | (2); and
-- src:39782 | (b) in any other case, for a period of 14 days from the day on
-- src:39783 | which the interim stop order is served.
@ref s 242(9) (src:39769-39783)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has revoked the interim stop order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority revoked the interim stop order?
    `the interim stop order was served during a hearing under subsection (4), or a hearing under subsection (4) was commenced while it was in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the interim stop order served during a hearing under section 242(4), or was a hearing under section 242(4) commenced while it was in force?
    `the Authority has made an order under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority made an order under section 242(1) or (2) by the day asked about?
    `the day the interim stop order was served` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the interim stop order served?
    `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you ask whether the interim stop order is in force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F24 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 242(9) the interim stop order is in force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the day the interim stop order was served`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An interim stop order ... is in force" speaks of an order that has been served
        IF `the Authority has revoked the interim stop order`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An interim stop order, unless revoked by the Authority, is in force"
        IF `the interim stop order was served during a hearing under subsection (4), or a hearing under subsection (4) was commenced while it was in force`
        THEN (IF `the Authority has made an order under subsection (1) or (2)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case where (i) it is served during a hearing under subsection (4); or (ii) a hearing under subsection (4) is commenced while it is in force, (a) until the Authority makes an order under subsection (1) or (2)"
        OTHERWISE (IF `the day asked about` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the day the interim stop order was served` 14 Days) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any other case, for a period of 14 days from the day on which the interim stop order is served"

-- s 242(10): subsections (5) and (7) do not apply where only an interim stop order has been served. A flat negative.
-- src:39785 | (10) Subsections (5) and (7) do not apply where only an interim
-- src:39786 | stop order has been served.
@ref s 242(10) (src:39785-39786)
GIVEN
    `only an interim stop order has been served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has only an interim stop order been served (and no stop order)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(10) subsections (5) and (7) apply` MEANS
    IF `only an interim stop order has been served`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (5) and (7) do not apply where only an interim stop order has been served"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative names the case where only an interim stop order has been served and says nothing of any other

§ `s 242(11) to (13): offences`

-- s 242(11): the offence of failing to comply with a stop order or an interim stop order, and its penalty.
-- src:39788 | (11) Any person who fails to comply with a stop order served under
-- src:39789 | subsection (1) or (2) or an interim stop order served under
-- src:39790 | subsection (8) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:39791 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $150,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:39792 | term not exceeding 2 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:39793 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $15,000 for every day or part
-- src:39794 | of a day during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 242(11) (src:39788-39794)
GIVEN
    `the person fails to comply with a stop order served under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to comply with a stop order served on you under section 242(1) or (2)?
    `the person fails to comply with an interim stop order served under subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to comply with an interim stop order served on you under section 242(8)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F25 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 242(11) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to comply with a stop order served under subsection (1) or (2)` OR `the person fails to comply with an interim stop order served under subsection (8)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who fails to comply with a stop order served under subsection (1) or (2) or an interim stop order served under subsection (8) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 242(11) (the penalty) (src:39788-39794)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 242(11) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 150000, 24, TRUE, 15000  -- a fine not exceeding $150,000, or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (24 months), or both; a further fine not exceeding $15,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

-- The order as a bar: no or no further securities or securities-based derivatives contracts may be allotted, issued or sold while a stop order or interim stop order is in force.
-- src:39598 | the Authority may by a written order (called in this section a stop
-- src:39599 | order) served on the person making the offer of securities or
-- src:39600 | securities‑based derivatives contracts to which the prospectus relates
-- src:39605 | direct that no or no further securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:39606 | contracts be allotted, issued or sold.
@ref s 242(1) (the order as a rule) (src:39598-39606)
GIVEN
    `the person making the offer` IS A Party @desc Who makes the offer?
    `a stop order or an interim stop order served on the person is in force` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc Is a stop order served on you under section 242(1) or (2), or an interim stop order served under section 242(8), in force? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 242 action`
`s 242(11) the person making the offer shall not allot, issue or sell contrary to the order` MEANS
    IF `a stop order or an interim stop order served on the person is in force` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the person making the offer`
         SHANT `s 242(11) allot, issue or sell securities or securities-based derivatives contracts contrary to the order`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person making the offer` BECAUSE "securities or securities-based derivatives contracts were allotted, issued or sold contrary to a stop order or an interim stop order; section 242(11) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 242(12): the offence of contravening subsection (5) or (7), and its penalty. The gate and the payment answers of the four paragraphs are passed in.
-- src:39796 | (12) Any person who contravenes subsection (5) or (7) shall be
-- src:39797 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:39802 | exceeding $100,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:39803 | further fine not exceeding $10,000 for every day or part of a day
-- src:39804 | during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 242(12) (src:39796-39804)
GIVEN
    `whether the person is bound by section 242(5)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 242(5)(a) the person making the offer is bound by paragraph (a)` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person has paid under section 242(5)(a)(ii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 242(5)(a)(ii) the person making the offer has paid the applicants within 14 days from the date of the stop order` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person is bound by section 242(5)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 242(5)(b) the person making the offer is bound by paragraph (b)` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person has paid under section 242(5)(b)(ii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 242(5)(b)(ii) the person making the offer has paid the applicants within 14 days from the date of the stop order` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person is bound by section 242(7)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 242(7)(a) the person making the offer is bound by paragraph (a)` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person has paid under section 242(7)(a)(ii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 242(7)(a)(ii) the person making the offer has paid the applicants within 14 days from the date of the stop order` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person is bound by section 242(7)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 242(7)(b) the person making the offer is bound by paragraph (b)` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person has acted under section 242(7)(b)(i)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 242(7)(b)(i) the person making the offer has informed the applicants and paid them, where title documents were issued` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person has paid under section 242(7)(b)(ii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 242(7)(b)(ii) the person making the offer has paid the applicants within 7 days, where no title documents were issued` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F26 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 242(12) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ((`whether the person is bound by section 242(5)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`whether the person has paid under section 242(5)(a)(ii)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) OR ((`whether the person is bound by section 242(5)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`whether the person has paid under section 242(5)(b)(ii)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) OR ((`whether the person is bound by section 242(7)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`whether the person has paid under section 242(7)(a)(ii)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) OR ((`whether the person is bound by section 242(7)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND ((`whether the person has acted under section 242(7)(b)(i)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`whether the person has paid under section 242(7)(b)(ii)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF ((`whether the person is bound by section 242(5)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`whether the person has paid under section 242(5)(a)(ii)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND ((`whether the person is bound by section 242(5)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`whether the person has paid under section 242(5)(b)(ii)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND ((`whether the person is bound by section 242(7)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`whether the person has paid under section 242(7)(a)(ii)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND ((`whether the person is bound by section 242(7)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR ((NOT (`whether the person has acted under section 242(7)(b)(i)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) AND (NOT (`whether the person has paid under section 242(7)(b)(ii)` EQUALS JUST FALSE))))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes subsection (5) or (7) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer under subsection (5) or (7) was not worked out

@ref s 242(12) (the penalty) (src:39796-39804)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 242(12) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 100000, 0, FALSE, 10000  -- a fine not exceeding $100,000; no imprisonment is stated (0); a further fine not exceeding $10,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

-- s 242(13): the reference to a statement in subsections (1)(a) and (2)(a) includes information presented in any form.
-- src:39806 | (13) For the purposes of subsections (1)(a) and (2)(a), any
-- src:39807 | reference to a statement includes a reference to any information
-- src:39808 | presented, regardless of whether such information is in text or
-- src:39809 | otherwise.
@ref s 242(13) (src:39806-39809)
GIVEN
    `the information is presented, whether in text or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information presented in the prospectus or profile statement, whether in text or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(13) the information presented is a statement for the purposes of subsections (1)(a) and (2)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the information is presented, whether in text or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "any reference to a statement includes a reference to any information presented" lists without closing the list
